#
# The public keys allowed to sign `assets/symbols/signed.toml`, in the OpenSSH
# allowed-signers format: one line per principal, never the private key.
#
#   cristian@punchisoft ssh-ed25519 AAAA...
#
# The owner adds their own key here; the agent prepares the manifest and commits the
# signature, but the private key never enters the repository or a session. Rotating the
# key means adding the new one, re-signing the manifest, and only then removing the old
# line, because removing it invalidates the signatures made with it.
